{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass in the days of Amraphel king of Shinar</b> This event happened to Abraham to teach that four kingdoms will arise to rule the world, and in the end his descendants will prevail over them and all of them will fall by their hand, and they will restore all their captives and their property. And the first among them was the king of Babylon, for so it was destined to be, as it is written (Daniel 2:38), \"You are the head of gold,\" and perhaps \"Ellasar\" is the name of a city in Media or in Persia, and \"Elam\" — in that city the king of Greece was crowned, he being the first king, and from there his kingdom spread when Darius was defeated. And our Sages already mentioned this (Avodah Zarah 10a): Rabbi Yosei says, they ruled in Elam for six years, and afterward their dominion spread throughout the entire world. And \"king of nations\" — he was crowned over diverse peoples who appointed him over them as head and commander, an allusion to the Roman king, who was crowned over a city gathered from many peoples — Kittim and Edom and other nations. And so they said in Bereshit Rabbah (Genesis Rabbah 42:2), Rabbi Avin said: just as He began with four kingdoms, so He does not conclude except with four kingdoms, etc. And there further (42:4 with variant wording): \"And it came to pass in the days of Amraphel king of Shinar\" — this is Babylon; \"Arioch king of Ellasar\" — this is Media; \"Chedorlaomer king of Elam\" — this is Greece; \"and Tidal king of nations\" — this is the kingdom of Edom, which is the inscription of tyranny over all the nations of the world."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The Aramaic phrase מכתבת טירוניא (from the midrash) is rendered literally as 'inscription of tyranny'; the term refers to Rome/Edom's coercive rule."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:28:20.044557835Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}